# `#[put]`

<SymbolMeta />
<SymbolSignature />

PUT shorthand for `#[route(PUT, path, ...)]` inside an HTTP `#[handlers]` implementation.

```rust
#[put("/{id}")]
async fn replace(&self, Path(id): Path<u64>, Json(input): Json<User>) -> Json<User> { todo!() }
```

It accepts an optional controller-relative string path followed by the shared route modifiers. `#[put]` and `#[put(streamed)]` mount at the controller base. It is a consumed marker, not a standalone function attribute. See [`#[route]`](./route) for complete grammar, modifier rules, containment, generated artifacts, and feature behavior.
